Unapplied activation artifact: staged broker runtime foundations
===============================================================

This patch is NOT sufficient by itself to compile the broker or expose it to
native catalog users. It remains unapplied against the active persistent-reap baseline.

Apply only after the coordinated source gate, alongside
broker-session-activation.patch and the still-required shared codec extraction:
- session_wire Frame visibility, read_frame_bytes, MessageAssembler(limit) with
  push/finish/has_seen/is_active, Sending new/next_frame/mark_sent.
- Apply broker-spool-activation.patch before the codec extraction; preserve its
  Sending::from_payload and joined serialization path.
- Preserve ordinary framing, parser strictness, send fences and existing tests.
- Implement ComponentServer broker handshake/DependencyClient demux, per-request
  dependency scopes, owned callback failure/EOF/disconnect cleanup before use.
- Update Cargo.lock and repository-required Bazel dependency/build metadata when
  adding UUID, then run linked tests. No broker tests have been compiled yet.

This patch only links staged modules/exports, adds UUID v4, transfers spool
ownership for the joined decoder. The explicit child reap helper is already
crate-visible in the active persistent-reap baseline. Broker reverse request parameters have an explicit
8 MiB cap and typed request_too_large error before parsing/handler admission;
ordinary history and broker response payloads remain uncapped.

